 "text": "Hi! How's everything today? That's likely. Fine dining places expect you to look well turned out, but they want you to enjoy yourself too. They' there for a reason. A good host will guide you through them, and the staff will mostly ignore the food on your plate. Many places have a simple rule, no jeans, and nothing too baggy. A nice pair of trousers is all you need. Ask the waiter or chef to explain, and they' happily help. It' all part of the experience. No need. The main course is usually the one that takes most time. The starters are often just for taste.",
